# --- Amazon S3, recipe photographs ---
# The bucket is private; the API hands out time-limited links, so nothing in
# it is publicly readable.
# Credentials: on your laptop, set the two AWS_ keys below. On EC2, leave them
# out entirely — the instance role supplies them and no secret sits on disk.
#
# S3_BUCKET=<the private photos bucket>
# AWS_REGION=ap-southeast-2
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<from the IAM user>
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<from the IAM user>

# Signs login tokens. Any long random string for development.
# Generate a different one for the deployed server:  openssl rand -hex 32
